# Archetype and engine reference, generated by tools/concordia/strategies/build_strategies.py (do not hand-edit). Full data: strategies/strategies.json.
# Engine goals apply to nearly every deck; an archetype row lists its role slots as role:min-max (a role with no count is a signal only). niche = thin archetype that borrows its crossover parents' fit.
engine[4|]{role|count|signals|note}:
  recursion|2-5|recursion+reanimate+from_zone:graveyard|baseline for every deck; no per-colour split; black decks and the graveyard archetypes run more (see recursion_by_archetype)
  ramp|10-12|mana_source+land_tutor+fixing|sources at 2 mana or less first; big_mana and lands_matter archetypes go higher
  card_draw|8-12|draw+draw_count|counted with selection; control and draw-heavy archetypes go higher
  protection|3-6|protection_trick+regenerate+protection_from+grant_kw:protection+phase_out+kw:hexproof+kw:indestructible+kw:protection|protect the commander and the engine; voltron; equipment; tokens; counters; combo; infect run more (see protection_by_archetype)
engine_uplift: recursion graveyard 8-12; reanimator 8-12; self_mill 8-12; aristocrats 4-8; blink 3-6; landfall 2-3; lands_matter 2-3; mill 4-8 | protection voltron 6-10; equipment 6-10; tokens 6-10; counters 6-10; combo 6-10; infect 6-10
removal: one family `remove:*` (destroy, exile, bounce, tuck, sacrifice); a card counts 1 whether it hits one creature or any number
archetypes[45|]{id|plan|roles|crossover|colors}:
  aristocrats|cheap recursive bodies feed a free outlet while death triggers drain; draw and make Treasure|fodder:10-12,outlet:5-8,payoff:8-10,card_adv:8-10,edict:6-8,recursion:-||B+WB+BR+BG+WBR
  tokens|go wide; double output; then one large alpha strike or a non-combat damage payoff|generator:10-14,doubler:2-4,anthem:4-6,finisher:-,drain:-,draw:6-8,protection:3-5,ramp:8-10||GW+WB+RG+UR+RGW
  tribal|density of one creature type; lords stack multiplicatively; payoffs reward casting or attacking with the type|lord:-,cost_reducer:-,card_adv:-,anthem:-,protection:-,recursion:-||any
  voltron|one protected threat (usually the commander) wins by 21 commander damage; often in two swings|attach:12-18,attach_helper:4-6,protection:6-8,evasion:-,tutor:-,ramp:8-10,damage_multiplier:-||RW+WU+GW+UR
  equipment|weapons are the engine that makes ordinary creatures real attackers; gear spreads across a team|equipment:10-14,tutor:-,cost_reducer:-,draw:-,carrier:12-18,protection:6-10||W+RW+R
  reanimator|stock the graveyard with a 7+ mana creature then reanimate it for 2-3 mana on turn 2-4|enabler:6-8,reanimation:8-12,target:6-10,protection:-||B+UB+WB+BG
  graveyard|the graveyard is a second hand: fill it; then recur many small resources (creatures; lands; spells)|filler:8-10,recursion:8-12,payoff:-,backup_engine:1-2||BG+BGU+UB+WBG
  mill|empty libraries (three opponents: repeatable and doubled mill) or cash in stocked graveyards|engine:8-12,doubler:2-3,payoff:-,outlet:-,interaction:8-10,graveyard_exile:-||U+UB+BGU
  spellslinger|many cheap instants and sorceries each turn feed per-cast payoffs|payoff:6-10,cantrip:8-12,cost_reducer:-,copy:-,rebuy:-,spells:25-35||UR+UBR+URW
  storm|bank many cheap spells in one turn until the storm count is lethal|cantrip:-,ritual:-,cost_reducer:-,refuel:-,payoff:2-3,spells:25-35||UR+UBR+R
  combo|tutor; protect; win in one decisive moment; 2-3 compact combos with redundancy|tutor:5-10,draw_select:8-12,enabler:-,payoff_engine:2-3,protection:6-10,remove:-||UB+UR+WB+BG
  counters|grow creatures with +1/+1 counters and multiply them until the weakest creature is huge|multiplier:3-5,enabler:15-20,proliferate:4-8,seed:-,draw_payoff:6-8,protection:3-5,ramp:8-10||GW+GU+WBG
